@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 Everything here uses made-up data and loopback addresses only. No real model, mail or CRM service is ever called.
 Run every tool from the repository root with `PYTHONPATH=src:.` (on Windows use `;` between the entries: `src;.`), as in the other run commands in contract.md.
 
+Every file path you give a tool on its command line (`--log`, `--facts`, `--requests`, `--book`, `--catcher`, `--crm`, `--model-log`, `--drain`, `--json`, `--out`, `--control`) must lie inside the folder you started it in, the repository folder, or the system temporary folder; a path that leaves them (`..`, an absolute path elsewhere, a link that points out) is refused with a message that names the option, and nothing is read or written. To use another folder, name it in the environment variable `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS` (several folders separated by `:`, or `;` on Windows). A NEW output file may only use letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-` in its name (a file that already exists may have any name except one with a control character; a new name that ends with a dot or is a Windows device name such as `nul`, `aux`, `con`, `prn`, `com1` or `lpt1`, with or without an extension, is refused on every system, so the file also opens on Windows). A file that is read and does not exist is reported as "no such file". A name with accented letters is found also when it is written in the other Unicode form (macOS stores `é` as two characters, other systems as one), below the allowed folder (upper and lower case must match on macOS, and the allowed folder itself must be written the way the system reports it). The same rule applies to `scripts/n8n_api.py import FILE` and `tools/scrub_n8n_export.py` (an n8n export kept in another folder, for example Downloads, is read after you copy it into the repository folder or list its folder in `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS`).
+
+Not covered, on purpose: `scripts/run_real_check.py` reads its config from any folder (the documentation tells you to keep it outside the repository) and uses the paths named inside it as written, and `scripts/run_live_check.py` takes its key file and its spend ledger from any folder for the same reason (`docs/real-services.md`). The config of `run_real_check.py` is found by looking the name up in the folder listings from the top of the file system, so it must be a file in a folder you can list: a config below a folder that you can enter but not list (mode 0711 owned by another user), or one handed over as `--config <(command)` or `/dev/fd/N`, is refused with a message; copy it to a normal file first. What this check is: a fence against a WRONG argument (a faulty script, a copied path). It is not a defence against an agent or a person who controls the shell: they can start the tool in another folder or set `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS`. The allowed folders are wide, and a file that already exists in one of them (the repository, the shared system temporary folder) can be overwritten by an output option that names it: the check does not know which files in them matter. It does not stop another process that swaps a folder for a link between the check and the open. The tools also start directly (`python load_tools/load_driver.py --help`, `python tools/scrub_n8n_export.py in.json out.json`) without setting `PYTHONPATH`.
+
 | File | What it does |
 |---|---|
 | `load_driver.py` | Sends requests to the desk's `POST /leads` on a fixed schedule and writes the **request log**. |
